# GraphCraft Rules (v0.1)

GraphCraft extends GraphStack. Both rule sets are active in this project.

## Activation

On session start, also read (once):
- `orchestrator/GRAPHCRAFT.md`
- `graphcraft-out/DESIGN_REPORT.md` (if exists)
- `graphcraft.config.yaml`
- `handoff/AESTHETIC_BRIEF.md` (if design task active)

## Graph layers

| Layer | Query |
|-------|-------|
| Code | `python -m graphstack graph query "..."` |
| Design | `python -m graphcraft design query "..."` |

## Role extensions

| Role | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Design Strategist | `.cursor/skills/design-strategist/DESIGN_STRATEGIST.md` |
| Designer | `.cursor/skills/designer/DESIGNER.md` |
| Stitch import | `.cursor/skills/stitch-import/STITCH_IMPORT.md` |
| Visual Review | `.cursor/skills/visual-review/VISUAL_REVIEW.md` |
| Mobile app | `.cursor/skills/mobile-app/MOBILE_APP.md` |
| Mobile game | `.cursor/skills/mobile-game/MOBILE_GAME.md` |

## Before UI code edits

1. `python -m graphcraft design update .` if design files changed
2. Confirm screen exists in design graph
3. GraphStack builder role + task in doing/ still required

## Profiles

Check `graphcraft.config.yaml`:
- `profile: mobile-app` → app stacks
- `profile: mobile-game` → game meta-UI focus

## Stitch mode

When `design_source: stitch|hybrid`:
- `.stitch/designs/*.png` = visual ground truth
- Run `python -m graphcraft stitch import .` after Stitch export
